# locks.dic — access-control / lock vendor default keys (Fase 2, familia "locks")
#
# Product-specific default keys used by some electronic locks and access-control
# systems that never got personalised. This is the "vendor" tier: lower
# probability than factory/transport defaults, tried after them.
#
# ⚠ AUTHORIZED USE ONLY. Like the rest of `check`, this only tries keys you
# already have against a card you are permitted to test. It performs no
# cryptographic attack.
#
# This shipped set is intentionally small and generic: sequential/example
# defaults that already appear in the open public dictionaries. Real
# engagement-specific vendor sets are curated by the operator — drop your own
# `<vendor>.dic` in this folder and register it in dicts.py, or pass it ad hoc
# with `--dict-file <path>`. Provenance/licence: see dicts/README.md.
#
# Format: one 12-hex key per line; `#` comments and blanks ignored (load_keys).

010203040506
123456789ABC
1122334455AA
# Example/demonstration entry (not a real product key): shows a card opening
# with a vendor-only key the factory dictionary does not contain.
A1B2C3D4E5F6
